WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Many cells in your body
could still divide.

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.430
Right now, most of them aren't.

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.810
They hold back.

4
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.640
Division happens on
demand, not on autopilot.

5
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.690
So what keeps a cell that
could divide in check,

6
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.260
until a new cell is really needed?

7
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.770
In this mission, you'll meet the
genes that control the cycle,

8
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.380
and find out what happens
when a mutation disables one.

9
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.820
Then you'll use what you've learned to
explain why the risk of most cancers rises

10
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.640
steeply with age.

11
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:34.560
Your mission: find out what keeps
cells that could still divide in check,

12
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.630
most of the time.
